From: sunshineinabox <aqemail@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: gcc-sm8650: add the 37.5 and 50 MHz SDCC2 rates

The SDCC2 apps RCG uses floor ops and lists only 400 kHz, 25, 100 and
202 MHz, so an SD card in High Speed or SDR25 (50 MHz) runs at 25 MHz,
and so does the 37.5 MHz that max-sd-hs-hz asks for on boards with an
SD level shifter. Add GPLL0_OUT_EVEN / 8 and / 6, as gcc-sm8550 and
gcc-sm8750 have and the vendor gcc-pineapple does.
---
 drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm8650.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm8650.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm8650.c
@@ -1240,6 +1240,8 @@
 static const struct freq_tbl ftbl_gcc_sdcc2_apps_clk_src[] = {
 	F(400000, P_BI_TCXO, 12, 1, 4),
 	F(25000000, P_GCC_GPLL0_OUT_EVEN, 12, 0, 0),
+	F(37500000, P_GCC_GPLL0_OUT_EVEN, 8, 0, 0),
+	F(50000000, P_GCC_GPLL0_OUT_EVEN, 6, 0, 0),
 	F(100000000, P_GCC_GPLL0_OUT_EVEN, 3, 0, 0),
 	F(202000000, P_GCC_GPLL9_OUT_MAIN, 4, 0, 0),
 	{ }
